  abstract = {In sociological discussions of the relation between the individual and modern society the identity of modern man is traditionally characterized as defective ('alienation', , the homeless mind'). Such characterization is mainly due to the assumption of a form of identity that fits the structure of medieval society but not the specific structure of modern society. In contrast the aim of this paper is to work out the theoretical idea of a correspondence between the form of society and the form of identity of members of society. While in medieval society, which is mainly shaped by stratification, a subatantial-teleological identity is appropriate, in functionally differentiated modern society a reflective-subjectivistic identity is required.},
  keywords = {⛔ No DOI found}
}

